# Read by citation("dwellr"). Every field that can be derived from DESCRIPTION
# is derived, so the entry cannot fall behind the package: the sibling packages
# carried hand-written copies in their READMEs and one of them cited a version
# three releases old before anyone noticed. `meta` is the DESCRIPTION, supplied
# by R when this file is read.
#
# The year is the year of first commit rather than of the current version, so
# it identifies the work and not the release being cited. The version is what
# distinguishes releases, and it is in the note.
#
# The author is the form all three packages now carry in Authors@R, so a
# bibliography holding more than one of them lists one author rather than two
# spellings of the same person. It is not the form on the book's cover, which
# is the full name and stays that way.

bibentry(
  bibtype = "Manual",
  title   = paste0(meta$Package, ": ", gsub("\\s+", " ", meta$Title)),
  author  = person("Ariel", "R. H."),
  year    = "2026",
  note    = paste("R package version", meta$Version),
  url     = paste0("https://github.com/ambientpointcorp/", meta$Package)
)
